@startuml UC-22 View Blog Post Detail - Sequence Diagram (stereo)
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #000000
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #000000
skinparam ArrowColor #000000
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 280

actor "Teacher or Moderator" as User
participant ":BlogCommunityPage" as UI <<user interaction>>
participant ":BlogController" as CTL <<coordinator>>
participant ":BlogPostService" as SVC <<business logic>>
participant ":BlogPostRepository" as POSTS <<interface>>
participant ":BlogCommentRepository" as COMMENTS <<interface>>
database DB

autonumber
User ->> UI : Select a published blog post in the Blog list
activate UI
UI ->> UI : loadDetail(id)
UI ->> CTL : GET /api/blog-posts/{id}
activate CTL
CTL ->> SVC : getDetail(id)
activate SVC
SVC ->> POSTS : findPublishedById(id)
activate POSTS
POSTS ->> DB : SELECT * FROM blog_posts WHERE id = ? AND status = 'PUBLISHED'
activate DB
DB -->> POSTS : row / none
deactivate DB
POSTS -->> SVC : BlogPost
deactivate POSTS

alt the post no longer exists or is no longer published
  SVC -->> CTL : ResourceNotFoundException
  CTL -->> UI : HTTP 404
  UI ->> UI : handleModeratorRemoved()
  UI -->> User : Show that the post is unavailable and return to the Blog screen

else the post or its discussion cannot be retrieved
  UI -->> User : Show MSG25 and let the user open the blog post again

else the post is published
  SVC ->> COMMENTS : findByPostId(postId)
  activate COMMENTS
  COMMENTS ->> DB : SELECT * FROM blog_comments WHERE post_id = ?\nAND the comment or one of its replies is not hidden ORDER BY created_at ASC
  activate DB
  DB -->> COMMENTS : rows
  deactivate DB
  COMMENTS -->> SVC : BlogComment [0..*]
  deactivate COMMENTS
  SVC ->> SVC : drop the hidden comments and the replies whose parent is hidden
  SVC ->> SVC : resolve the display name of the post author and of every comment author
  SVC -->> CTL : BlogPostDetail
  CTL -->> UI : HTTP 200 + BlogPostDetail
  UI ->> UI : group the replies under their parent comment
  UI ->> UI : decide which comment, owner and moderation actions the signed-in user may use
  UI -->> User : Show the title, body, author, subject tag, publication date, comments and permitted actions
end
deactivate SVC
deactivate CTL
deactivate UI
@enduml
